<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-READY-O4>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-READY-O4" ;
  triage:title "refresh_persisted_stats() overwrites (not sums into) timeline_dropped_persist_error_total, silently discarding bootstrap-side WriterClosed/InvalidBatch drop counts from /v1/health" ;
  triage:description "fenix-C architecture/boundaries review (01M1S751VVM0K4C7ZW6YDPC7BQ, their F4). quality-mgr confirmed by direct read: crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/diagnostic_timeline.rs:220-249 refresh_persisted_stats() does self.stats.timeline_dropped_persist_error_total.store(persistence.persist_error_total(), Ordering::Relaxed) -- an unconditional overwrite, not a sum -- discarding whatever flush_locked() had already fetch_add'd for bootstrap-side non-queue-full drops (WriterClosed/InvalidBatch). Those drops become invisible to /v1/health, a genuine counter-ownership / honest loss semantics bug: an operator watching health would see zero drops even while some occurred. Fix: sum the persisted-store count into the existing counter (fetch_add) instead of overwriting it, or maintain the two counters as clearly separate, distinctly-named metrics with a combined total exposed separately." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "observability-health" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
